--- fixture: data files and rows per Iceberg table
f	1	100000
fa	1	100000
fp	5	100000
--- T11 rule 1, identity partition: 5 values
Join: fp[100000] ⋈ d[1]
ResultRows: 20000
--- T11 rule 1 after partition pruning: 2 values in the surviving files
Join: fp[no_stats~40000] ⋈ d[1]
ResultRows: ~~20000
--- T11 rule 2, dense integer: range 2500
Join: f[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 400
--- T11 rule 2, sparse integer: range clamped to the rows
Join: f[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 10
--- T11 rule 3, Float64 without bounds
ResultRows equals the estimate from column_sizes / 8
--- T11 rule 3, Decimal(18, 2): bounds, but no range rule for decimals
ResultRows equals the estimate from column_sizes / 8
--- T11 rule 4, String: half the rows
Join: f[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 20
--- T11 rule 2 in an Avro data file
Join: fa[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 400
--- T11 rule 4, Float64 in an Avro data file without column_sizes: 30% of the rows
Join: fa[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 33
--- T17 use_statistics = 0: rows only
Join: f[100000] ⋈ d[no_stats~10]
ResultRows: ~~10
--- T17 use_iceberg_manifest_column_statistics = 0: rows only
Join: f[100000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 10
--- gate off
Join: f ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: unknown
